    // (group, context, lines). Plain string literals only (the generator parses this table).
    static let script2: [(String, String, [String])] = [
        // MARK: Townsfolk
        ("folk", "greet", ["Evening, friend. Or is it still afternoon? I lose track.", "Oh! You gave me a start.", "Back again? Town must agree with you.",
                           "Welcome. Don't mind the dust, it's everywhere.", "Ah, a new face. We don't get many.", "Hello. You look hungry. The saloon's that way.",
                           "Mind your step, the boardwalk's got a loose plank.", "Hey there. Nice hat.", "Well now, a traveller. Where'd you ride in from?",
                           "Morning. Did you hear the rooster? Everyone heard the rooster.", "Hi. Sorry, I'm in a hurry. Hello though.", "Good to see you again.",
                           "Afternoon. Hot enough for you?", "Ho there. Come to stay a while?", "Look who's still breathing. Glad of it.",
                           "Hey! Weren't you here last week? Thought so.", "Pleasure. Name's not important. Neither's mine.", "Oh, hello. Lovely day for a walk.",
                           "You look like trouble. The good kind, I hope.", "Welcome to town. We've got one of everything. Mostly."]),
        ("folk", "chatter", ["My back's been aching since the rain.", "They're fixing the church bell. Finally.", "Somebody painted the water tower. Badly.",
                             "I've been meaning to fix my roof for three summers.", "The baker's got a new oven. You can smell it from here.",
                             "Heard a rattler got into the general store.", "Mail coach is late again.", "My neighbour's goat ate my washing.",
                             "They say the mine up north is cursed. They say a lot of things.", "I'm thinking about growing tomatoes. Big ones.",
                             "Somebody stole the bell rope. Who steals a rope?", "The river's been low. Fish are cranky.",
                             "My aunt's coming to visit. Pray for me.", "Lost a button. Looked all morning. It was on my other shirt.",
                             "If the wind keeps up, the windmill's going to fly off.", "Saw a hawk take a rabbit clean off the road.",
                             "I hear the Capital's building another wall. Walls everywhere.", "Somebody keeps ringing the fire bell for fun.",
                             "The new deputy's young. Means well, though.", "My boots are older than some of the folk here.",
                             "Saw a stranger on the ridge yesterday. Just watching.", "They found an old wagon wheel in the creek. Nobody knows whose.",
                             "My grandmother says it'll be a hard winter. She says that every year.", "I swear the clock on the bank runs fast.",
                             "Who keeps leaving apple cores on the fence?", "I'd go fishing but the fish know me now.",
                             "The doctor's away. Try not to break anything.", "Somebody's got a fiddle. Somebody can't play it.",
                             "Price of nails went up. Price of everything went up.", "There's a dance on Saturday. You should come.",
                             "Heard wolves last night out past the mill.", "The schoolteacher's got a cough. Kids are thrilled.",
                             "That cloud looks like a horse. No, a pig. A horse-pig.", "Our cat brought home a snake. Proud as anything.",
                             "My horse throws a shoe every time I go to market.", "They're digging a new well behind the chapel.",
                             "The bridge creaks. I walk faster on it.", "Somebody tried to sell me a map to buried gold. Twice.",
                             "Town meeting's on Thursday. Bring a chair.", "Best pie in the county is at the saloon. Don't tell the baker.",
                             "Heard gunfire up the valley this morning. Hunters, I hope.", "They say a soldier deserted and hides in the hills.",
                             "My son wants to join the Capital's army. I said eat your beans first.", "The well bucket's got a hole. Again.",
                             "Watched the sunset last night. Best one all year.", "There's a funny smell by the tannery. There always is.",
                             "Remember when the barn burned? Nobody's forgotten.", "Got a letter from my brother out east. Wants money, of course.",
                             "Whoever's playing the piano at night, please stop.", "They say there's a vault under the ash plains. I say nonsense.",
                             "Saw a man ride through with a rifle as long as he was tall.", "The undertaker's been idle. That's a good sign.",
                             "My dog only barks at the mailman. Nobody else.", "Seed's in. Now we wait and pray for rain.",
                             "Fresh paint on the post office. Looks right smart.", "They hanged a scarecrow by the road. Scared me too.",
                             "Some fellow came through selling tonic. Tasted like boot polish.", "Getting old's no fun. Better than the alternative.",
                             "If you need a wagon fixed, try the smith. He's slow but good.", "Haven't had a quiet week since spring.",
                             "Saw the train smoke way off on the plain.", "My wife says I talk too much. She's not wrong.",
                             "Heard a raid hit a homestead out west. Keep your eyes open.", "The church choir's practising. Mind your ears.",
                             "Somebody's chickens got loose. The whole street's chasing them.", "I owe the barber money. Don't tell him you saw me.",
                             "They say the old mine still has silver. They also say it caves in.", "Good wood's getting hard to find around here.",
                             "Rain's coming. My knee knows.", "I had a dream about cake last night. Woke up sad."]),
        ("folk", "night", ["Moon's up. Time I wasn't.", "Night air's good for thinking. And catching cold.", "Hear the crickets? Loud tonight.",
                           "Don't wander off the road in the dark.", "Lanterns are lit. Town looks pretty this time of night.", "Coyotes are singing again.",
                           "I'd stay in tonight, if I were you.", "Long day. Longer night.", "Owls are out. Mice should be in.",
                           "Strange shapes in the dark out past the fence.", "Keep your lamp trimmed, friend.", "The saloon gets rowdy this late.",
                           "Folks say things move in the fields at night.", "Cold one tonight. Wear a coat.", "Off to bed. Wake me if there's a fire.",
